1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 {Philidor's Defence is quite unusual, Peter decided to play
it because knowbody knows} 3. d4 Nd7 4. Nc3 $6 {That move is imprecise already,
better is to accelarate with Bc4} (4. Bc4 c6 5. O-O Be7 6. dxe5 dxe5 7. Ng5
Bxg5 8. Qh5 Qe7 9. Bxg5 {is according to theory and much better for White})
4... c6 5. Bc4 Be7 6. O-O b5 $5 7. Bb3 Ngf6 8. a3 $2 {This move turns out to
be poor} O-O 9. Be3 a5 {Now Black threatens b5-b4 and Nxe4} 10. d5 Bb7 11. dxc6
Bxc6 12. Bd5 $2 {A poor move} Qc7 13. Qd2 Rfc8 {Now Black has a strong
pressure on the c-file} 14. Ng5 Bxd5 15. Nxd5 Nxd5 16. Qxd5 Qc4 $1 {A fine
move - defending f7 and controlling the centre} 17. Rfd1 Rab8 18. f3 $2 {
Loses a pawn but White's position is on disadvantage already} (18. c3 Nf6 19.
Qxc4 bxc4 $1) 18... Qxd5 19. Rxd5 Rxc2 20. Rd2 {Now Black has a clear edge}
Rbc8 21. Rad1 R8c4 22. Nh3 Nc5 23. Bxc5 {Sad, but I didn't like the idea of Nb3
} Rxc5 24. Nf2 h5 25. Nd3 R5c4 26. Ne1 Rxd2 27. Rxd2 Kf8 28. Rc2 {The only
chance is to exchange rooks and to defend a worse endgame} Rc5 29. Kf2 Ke8 30.
Ke2 Kd7 31. b3 Kc6 32. a4 b4 33. Kd3 g6 {Both sides tried to improve their
positions. I put my pawns on the light square to minimize the effect of
Black's dark-squared bishop} 34. Rc4 d5 35. Rxc5+ Bxc5 36. Nc2 Bf2 37. Ke2 Bd4
38. Kd3 Kc5 39. Ke2 ({Fritz suggested} 39. Nxd4 dxe4+ 40. fxe4 exd4 {but this
loses after} 41. g3 g5 42. h3 f6 43. Kd2 Kd6 44. Ke2 Ke5 45. Kd3 h4 46. g4 Kf4)
39... f5 40. Kd3 Bf2 41. Ke2 $6 {Loses a second pawn} Bg1 42. h3 dxe4 43. fxe4
fxe4 44. Kf1 Bd4 45. Ke2 Kd5 46. Ne1 Bb6 47. Nc2 Bd8 48. Kf2 Bg5 49. Ke2 e3 50.
Kd3 e4+ 51. Ke2 Ke5 52. Kf1 Bh4 53. Ke2 Bf2 54. Kf1 Bh4 55. Ke2 Bg5 56. Kf1 Bd8
{A time loss after Black didn't find a way to manage the win} 57. Ke2 Bb6 58.
Kf1 Bc5 59. Ke2 Bd4 60. Kf1 Bc3 61. Ke2 Bd2 62. Kf1 h4 63. Ke2 g5 64. Kf1 Kf4
65. Ke2 Kg3 66. Kf1 Kh2 67. Nd4 Bc3 68. Nc6 e2+ 69. Kxe2 Kxg2 70. Nxa5 Bd4 71.
